A value carrying a macro call is rendered before it is typed: with the macro pinned by a
`macro_stubs:` mapping in fixture config nothing is executed, and the literal it resolves to
is coerced like any other value — a bare integer lands unquoted.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    build: ["false"]
macro_stubs:
  core.macros.build: "42"
-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md build="{{ macro('core.macros.build') }}"
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 ---
 title: Foo
+build: 42
 ---
 # Body
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: build=42
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
build: 42
---
# Body
